---
---
<section id="about" class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 z-10">

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 reveal">

    <!-- Bio -->
    <div class="md:col-span-12 space-y-5">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl text-white font-medium">
        About
      </h2>
      <p class="font-body text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        I'm a full-stack developer based in Addis Ababa. Most of my work starts on the backend —
        modeling the data, wiring up authentication, getting the API right — and moves out from
        there into a React front end. I also handle my own deployments, so a project isn't done
        until it's actually live and something I keep maintaining, not just code sitting in a repo.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Stack -->
    <div class="md:col-span-12 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8 pt-8 border-t border-white/10">
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-white text-base font-semibold">Backend</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Python, Django, Django REST Framework, relational schema design, SQL.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-white text-base font-semibold">Frontend</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          React, Next.js, Tailwind CSS.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-white text-base font-semibold">Tools &amp; deployment</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Git, Linux-hosted deployments, custom Django admin theming.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-white text-base font-semibold">How I work</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Start from the data model, build the API around it, then the interface — and stay on
          the project through deployment rather than handing it off half-finished.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>